Quick update on the rollback plan:

I've been working through failure scenarios. Here's what I have so far:

Scenario 1: Data corruption in new schema
  - Stop v2 traffic at load balancer
  - Run reverse migration script (tested on staging, takes ~4 min)
  - Redirect traffic back to v1
  - Estimated downtime: 6-8 minutes

Scenario 2: Performance degradation (>500ms p99)
  - Shift 100% traffic to v1 via feature flag (no downtime)
  - Investigate with v2 receiving shadow traffic only

Scenario 3: Partial failure (subset of endpoints)
  - Use per-endpoint routing rules to mix v1/v2
  - Already tested this config on staging

Still need to document Scenario 4 (auth service dependency failure).
Will have it done by tomorrow EOD.

- Dave

